meta {
  name: Unknown Section
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/home/xyz
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 404
  res.body.error.code: eq SECTION_NOT_FOUND
  res.body.error.message: contains Known sections
}

docs {
  # Unknown Section — 404
  
  A slug that is not a known section key:
  
  ```json
  {
    "error": {
      "code": "SECTION_NOT_FOUND",
      "message": "Unknown section 'nonsense'. Known sections: hero, trusted-by, about, solutions, pillar-detail, product-showcase, tech-stack."
    }
  }
  ```
  
  The message enumerates the valid slugs, so a client that gets this can
  recover without a second call to **List Sections**.
  
  Worth exercising: this is the path that proves error handling works
  end to end — thrown in the controller, formatted by a single error
  middleware, never leaking internals.
}
